Having played at least a hundred games with this patch, I'd have to
agree that it doesn't make much of a difference at all.

If anything, it decreases my frustration level in going from level to
level.  The only real "advantage" I can see is that I use a little
less food (4 or 5 turns worth at most) going up/down the stairs.  This
extra time might make a difference when you've got the Amulet and are
going back up the dungeon, but I think it's miniscule.  On the flip
side, I've definitely almost been killed more than once by a vampire
who followed me up the stairs from a distance.  If you turn a corner
and see a strong monster, it's a lot easier to use your speed to get
two squares ahead, but you need a good distance to the stairs to get a
full three so that it can't follow you. I'd say that it's almost
unbalancing /against/ the player.

The increased radius on the trapdoor is a little unbalancing for the
player however, because I keep my pet a lot more frequently than I
would otherwise have.

